WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.408
Because very few datasets provide annotated
explanations alongside answers,

00:00:04.488 --> 00:00:08.897
the authors chose the two largest available.

00:00:08.977 --> 00:00:13.385
GQA-REX contains explanations for roughly
ninety-eight percent of the samples in the GQA-balanced dataset,

00:00:13.465 --> 00:00:17.873
about 1.04 million question-answer pairs spanning
eighty-two thousand images,

00:00:17.953 --> 00:00:22.362
with one explanation per pair.

00:00:22.442 --> 00:00:26.850
However,

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:31.338
its explanations follow the reasoning-format of
prior work and are not fully human-readable,

00:00:31.418 --> 00:00:35.827
sometimes containing grammatical inaccuracies.

00:00:35.907 --> 00:00:40.315
VQA-E provides explanations for about forty percent
of the question-answer pairs in VQA 2.0,

00:00:40.395 --> 00:00:44.803
and because those explanations are built by
matching captions to the question-answer pair,

00:00:44.883 --> 00:00:49.292
they tend to read more like image captions than
genuine reasoning.

00:00:49.372 --> 00:00:53.780
Both datasets have limitations, which the authors
are transparent about.
